te  house medical office so that  the attending physician is going to be  having a really big role to play here  uh the white house put out a memo from  that physician  uh earlier to sort of walk through  what some of these procedures are but  this is really sort of a  a white house driven thing it's not as  if like just because  the white house is in the middle of the  district of columbia that all of a  sudden the mayor of dc  has a state that really isn't the case  here it's very much the white house the  federal government  if he needs medical attention walter  reed medical center is right the way up  uh certainly uh the with the military  and the department of defense there's  going to be the best  doctors that the u.s federal government  has at their disposal  all of the top research in that will be  available to president trump as he goes  through that  now right now it seems like as you and i  are sitting here  discussing this it seems like you know  he's doing as open as he can be right  now  you know let's let's as i say let's hope  and pray that that stays the same  but if things were to get worse there  are a lot of resources and assets that  are at the president's disposal  so of course we are concerned about the  president but also the people around him  uh we saw vp pence a tweet this earlier  sending his love and prayers to donald  trump and his wife  melania trump but let's talk a little  bit about what happens  um to the people around him and the next  presidential debate  wasn't he pretty close in contact with  uh biden for example what happens next  well you're going to see an aggressive  contact tracing  uh system that's already underway uh you  will see people who are close to  president trump to pope hicks get tested  now that's going to wind up being quite  a lot of people in the white house so it  is theoretically possible  that there will be more announcements to  come it'll also include  some members of congress who have  traveled with  donald trump to rallies recently and  then  you know one of the key things here is  going to be  to try and figure out how big this  spread is is it just  that the president and his wife and you  know one or two senior staffers  uh got diagnosed with this or is this a  bigger thing and what sort of knock-on  effects  uh did that have so that's gonna be one  of the key things now  former vice president joe biden his  campaign has protocols  to try and keep him safe at the debate  uh donald trump and joe biden were  actually pretty distant one from another  they were standing  on separate sides of the stage they  didn't shake hands  at the beginning there wasn't like a lot  of glad handing going on now they were  in the same  hall not everyone on the trump side was  wearing  a mask uh so so there is some  question here but the biden campaign  will have a protocol for  what you would do if someone close in  proximity to joe biden  were to get diagnosed with coping 19 i  would imagine  we will hear from them uh hopefully soon  but i would imagine that those protocols  would immediately  start going into effect right we haven't  seen any  tweets for example from biden yet but  hopefully we hear uh something and  are uh we'll keep you posted on the  latest so thank you so much derek for  joining us our bloomberg  senior editor and thank you all for  watching a quick take make sure to  follow us at clicktake and at business  for all the latest updates and more stay  tuned bye for now

